<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to
        be. Do not paste this back into <description>.

        Stage gate (a): a deal cannot enter LOI until the underwriting has been approved by
        the principals (UW_Approved__c).

        Safe against the legitimate route by construction: Underwriting_Approval's
        finalApprovalActions sets StageName = 'LOI' and UW_Approved__c = true in the same
        action set / same record save, so the flag is already true when this rule evaluates,
        true whether or not approval-process field updates run validation rules in this org.

        Gate applies to the stage transition only (ISCHANGED); existing records already at
        LOI are unaffected.

        Known, accepted: UW_Approved__c is never cleared, so a once-approved deal can be
        moved back into LOI manually forever, acceptable, since a deal that has been
        principal-approved once has passed the gate this rule exists to enforce.
    -->
    <fullName>Underwriting_Approved_Before_LOI</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks stage entry to LOI unless the underwriting has been approved by the principals (UW_Approved__c). See the XML comment in this file for full rationale.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISCHANGED(StageName),
    ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;LOI&apos;),
    NOT(UW_Approved__c)
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>StageName</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>This deal cannot enter LOI until the underwriting has been approved by the principals. Submit it for approval from the Underwriting stage.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
